# Executable production import fence (not a pytest collection claim)

This probe runs the production import head used by meeting intelligence:
`from holdspeak.intel import OpenAI`. It is run directly by each retained
isolated venv, with a fresh isolated HOME. No hub, model, endpoint, keychain,
microphone, or test suite is started.

## README/base installation — expected failure

Command:

```sh
probe_home=$(mktemp -d); export HOME="$probe_home"; baseline_venv=/var/folders/q7/5dzz5g2116b3lq8rhg7hwjrr0000gn/T/tmp.7N7LjZODSs; printf '%s\n' "HOME=$HOME" "VENV=$baseline_venv"; "$baseline_venv/bin/python" -c 'from holdspeak.intel import OpenAI; print(f"OpenAI={OpenAI!r}"); assert OpenAI is not None, "production OpenAI client is unavailable"'
```

Output:

```text
HOME=/var/folders/q7/5dzz5g2116b3lq8rhg7hwjrr0000gn/T/tmp.XQJ8RhWvCS
VENV=/var/folders/q7/5dzz5g2116b3lq8rhg7hwjrr0000gn/T/tmp.7N7LjZODSs
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "<string>", line 1, in <module>
    from holdspeak.intel import OpenAI; print(f"OpenAI={OpenAI!r}"); assert OpenAI is not None, "production OpenAI client is unavailable"
                                                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
AssertionError: production OpenAI client is unavailable
OpenAI=None
```

Exit status: `1`.

